; mstp_master.loom
;
; A BACnet MS/TP master node (ANSI/ASHRAE 135 clause 9: master-slave/
; token-passing on an RS-485 half-duplex bus, the building-automation
; field bus), as one program that two threads run at once, each with its
; own pins and its own data: two masters on one chip. A master takes part
; in the token ring of the addresses 0 .. Nmax_master: it finds its
; successor by Poll For Master, answers other masters' polls, sends one
; host frame (BACnet Data Not Expecting Reply) each time it holds the
; token, passes the token on, polls one more address every Npoll tokens
; (to find a master that has come up), retries a pass once and looks for
; a new successor when the old one stays silent, and makes a new token
; when the bus has been silent for Tno_token + TS * Tslot (lost-token
; recovery). It gives the host the data frames addressed to it or
; broadcast. RX comes from the RO output of an RS-485 transceiver, TX goes
; to its DI input and DE to its driver enable.
;
; Written on 2026-11-07, after the hardware was complete (D-032), as a
; protocol Loom was not designed for (D-035). It uses the M2 core (pins,
; deadlines, the FIFOs), LD/ST of slice B (SEMANTICS 6.11), built for the
; I2C EEPROM's array and USB's descriptors, here holding each master's
; settings, ring state, received header and frame to send, and the bit
; engine in manual mode (SEMANTICS 6.9) with its CRC unit, built for USB's
; CRC5/CRC16 and CAN's CRC15: both MS/TP CRCs (the header CRC-8,
; x^8 + x^7 + 1, and the data CRC-16, x^16 + x^12 + x^5 + 1, both
; reflected) run on it, one after the other in each frame, by feeding the
; bits LSB first into its MSB-first register and bit-reversing the result
; (REV), which is the same arithmetic. The code names no pin: TX and DE
; are written by OUT through the thread's OUTGRP, data bits leave by SHO
; and enter by SHI through its BE_PINS, and the start bit is found by IN
; through its INGRP, so the one copy of the code serves both threads (the
; 512-word memory has room for one copy and two masters' data, not for
; two copies). No hardware knows MS/TP or a UART: the characters, the
; start-bit search, the preamble hunt, the frame format, both CRCs' byte
; order and complement, the silence timers, the turnaround and the master
; node state machine are all firmware.
;
; Sources: clause 9 is not free. The frame format, both CRCs and the
; master state machine follow the open-source BACnet stack (S. Karg,
; bacnet-stack, src/bacnet/datalink/mstp.c, mstp.h, mstpdef.h, crc.c),
; a secondary source; tools/protomodels/mstp.py is the model and cites them.
;
; Pins: master 0 (thread 0) RX = IN0, TX = OUT0, DE = OUT1; master 1
; (thread 2) RX = IN2, TX = OUT2, DE = OUT3. TX idles high; DE = 1 drives
; the bus. All six move with the assembler's --pin, TX to an OUT pin and
; DE to the pin after it (OUT writes the two together). The bench or the
; board wires the two transceivers to one bus.
;
; Settings, words of data memory the host loads with the image, before RUN
; (master 0 at CFG0, master 1 at CFG2; ticks are eighths of a bit):
;     +0   TS, this station's address, 0 .. Nmax_master
;     +1   Nmax_master, 1 .. 127
;     +2   Tusage_timeout in ticks, 1 .. 65535 (20 .. 35 ms; at 9600 baud
;          20 ms is 1536 ticks): how long a pass or a poll waits for the
;          other station to start a frame
;     +3   TL, +4 NL: the silence after which this station makes a new
;          token, Tno_token + TS * Tslot (500 ms + TS * 10 ms), as NL
;          periods of TL ticks (1 .. 65535 each)
;     +5   Tframe_abort in ticks (60 bit times = 480 ticks): the longest
;          silence between two octets of a frame
;     +6   Npoll (50): tokens between two maintenance polls
; A frame's first octet is waited for from when the master starts to
; listen (just after the frame before, sent or received; IDLE starts again
; after every frame it sees); later octets from the middle of the stop bit
; of the octet before. Rate: eight ticks a bit, TICK_INT and
; TICK_FRAC set by the host before RUN; the pairs are proved for ticks of
; 24 clocks or more (192 clocks a bit, 260 kbaud at 50 MHz; MS/TP runs at
; 9600 .. 115200 baud, 54 .. 651 clocks a tick).
;
; Host frame (INQ), sent the next time the token is held:
;     word 1     bits 7:0 the destination (255 broadcast), bits 15:8 n,
;                1 .. 29 bytes of data
;     n words    the data, one byte per word in bits 7:0
; It goes out as a BACnet Data Not Expecting Reply frame (type 6). The
; whole frame must reach INQ promptly once the token is held: the node
; waits for it while the bus stays silent.
; Report (OUTQ):
;     0x40dd     the host frame went out, to station dd
;     0x00bb     a data byte of a frame received with DA = TS or 255
;     status     after those bytes: bit 15 set, bit 14 the data CRC is
;                bad, bits 13:8 the frame type, bits 7:0 the source
; A byte or status that finds OUTQ full is dropped: the host keeps OUTQ
; drained.
;
; Not done (weaker than a full clause 9 node): no Data Expecting Reply is
; sent and none is answered (no ANSWER_DATA_REQUEST, no Reply Postponed; a
; requester times out), Test_Request is not answered, Nmax_info_frames is
; 1, frames over 29 data bytes are not sent (any length is received), the
; stop bits received are not checked (the CRCs are), and the start bit is
; found on the tick grid, so a received bit is sampled 0 to 1 tick (an
; eighth of a bit) before its middle. A frame that follows the one before
; with little idle is received only if the master is back at rxframe, and
; sees the line at mark, before its first start bit; the tests send one
; bit of idle at 192 clocks a bit (a model master's data frame, then its
; Token); no idle at all is not tested. A frame after a turnaround is
; always seen.
;
; Memory: the code is in thread 0's section, 0x000 .. 0x0FF and from
; 0x110 on; thread 2's entry, 0x100 .. 0x10F, sets its pins and jumps into
; it. Threads 1 and 3 must not be started. Data: master 0 at 0x1A0, master
; 1 at 0x1D0, 48 words each (the settings, the ring state, the received
; header, the frame to send); the image need not load more than the
; settings.
;
; Readings taken on the open spec questions (2026-11-07): ASHRAE 135
; clause 9 was not read; timing and CRCs from an open-source BACnet
; stack (secondary). The CRC polynomial names are from memory; a test
; shows the stack's code equals the reflected CRCs of those polynomials.
;   Any octet that starts within Tusage_timeout counts as the successor
;   using the token (the stack asks for more than 4 octets).
;   A sole master polls the ring again after every token use.
;   A partial master: no Data Expecting Reply, no Test_Request answer,
;   one frame per token, host frames of 1 to 29 bytes, stop bits not
;   checked (the CRCs are).

        .imem   512                     ; the macro build: quarters of 128 words
        .pins   RX = IN0, TX = OUT0, DE = OUT1
        .pins   RX2 = IN2, TX2 = OUT2, DE2 = OUT3
        .tick   24                      ; the shortest tick the pairs are proved for
        .equ    OVS = 8                 ; ticks per bit
        .equ    CFG0 = 0x1A0            ; master 0's data; r1 holds it
        .equ    CFG2 = 0x1D0            ; master 1's data
        .equ    TS = 0                  ; the settings
        .equ    NMAX = 1
        .equ    TUSE = 2
        .equ    TL = 3
        .equ    NL = 4
        .equ    TABRT = 5
        .equ    NPOLL = 6
        .equ    NS = 7                  ; the ring state
        .equ    PS = 8
        .equ    TC = 9
        .equ    RETRY = 10
        .equ    CNTL = 11               ; NL periods left
        .equ    STATE = 12              ; where rxframe returns
        .equ    HDR = 13                ; type, DA, SA, length (2), CRC
        .equ    BUF = 19                ; the frame to send, 29 bytes
        .equ    T_TOKEN = 0             ; frame types
        .equ    T_PFM = 1
        .equ    T_RPFM = 2
        .equ    T_DNER = 6

; Registers: r0 an octet or scratch, r1 the master's data (CFG0 or CFG2),
; r2 a frame type or a pointer, r3 a station address or a count, r4 a data
; length, r5 a timeout in ticks (rxbyte's argument), r6 scratch, r7 the
; .csr scratch.

; Each thread's entry: its pins, then the one copy of the code. OUTGRP is
; TX and DE (bit 0 TX, bit 1 DE), INGRP is RX alone.
        .thread 2
        .csr    OUTGRP, (2 << 5) | pin(TX2)
        .csr    INGRP, (1 << 5) | pin(RX2)
        .csr    BE_PINS, (pin(RX2) << 5) | pin(TX2)
        MOV16   r1, CFG2
        JMP     start

        .thread 0
        .csr    OUTGRP, (2 << 5) | pin(TX)
        .csr    INGRP, (1 << 5) | pin(RX)
        .csr    BE_PINS, (pin(RX) << 5) | pin(TX)
        MOV16   r1, CFG0
start:  LDI     r0, 1
        OUT     r0                      ; TX mark, DE off: listen
        .csr    BE_CFG, 0x200           ; NRZ, LSB first, CRC_EN
        LD      r0, r1, TS              ; INITIALIZE: NS = PS = TS,
        ST      r0, r1, NS              ; TokenCount = Npoll
        ST      r0, r1, PS
        LD      r0, r1, NPOLL
        ST      r0, r1, TC
        SETD    0                       ; the silence starts now

; ------------------------------------------------------------------- IDLE
; Wait for a frame. A silence of Tno_token + TS * Tslot is NO_TOKEN run
; out: every station waits Tno_token, then Tslot more for each address
; below its own, so the lowest address that is alive makes the token.
idle:   LD      r0, r1, NL
        ST      r0, r1, CNTL
idlew:  LD      r5, r1, TL
        LDI     r0, 1                   ; rxframe returns to idlec
        ST      r0, r1, STATE
        JMP     rxframe
idlec:  BNT     seen
        LD      r0, r1, CNTL
        DEC     r0
        ST      r0, r1, CNTL
        BNZ     idlew
        JMP     lost
seen:   BNZ     idle                    ; an invalid frame
seenv:  LD      r2, r1, HDR + 1         ; a valid one: DA
        LD      r3, r1, TS
        CMP     r2, r3
        BNZ     idle                    ; not for us (data for 255 is reported)
        LD      r0, r1, HDR             ; the type
        TEST    r0, r0
        BZ      usetok                  ; Token: USE_TOKEN
        CMPI    r0, T_PFM
        BNZ     idle                    ; data frames went to the host already
        LDI     r2, T_RPFM              ; Poll For Master: Reply To Poll For Master
        LD      r3, r1, HDR + 2
        LDI     r4, 0
        CALL    txframe
        JMP     idle

; PASS_TOKEN's successor silent twice: the same from NS + 1 (ptfail).
lost:   LD      r0, r1, TS
        ST      r0, r1, PS
lostps: LD      r0, r1, TS
        ST      r0, r1, NS
        LDI     r0, 0
        ST      r0, r1, TC
        JMP     pollps
pollts: LD      r0, r1, TS              ; PS = TS, poll from TS + 1
        ST      r0, r1, PS
pollps:
        LD      r3, r1, PS              ; r3 = (PS + 1) mod (Nmax_master + 1)
        INC     r3
        LD      r0, r1, NMAX
        CMP     r0, r3
        BC      np1
        LDI     r3, 0
np1:
poll:   ST      r3, r1, PS              ; Poll For Master to r3 = PS
        LDI     r2, T_PFM
        LDI     r4, 0
        CALL    txframe

; -------------------------------------------------------- POLL_FOR_MASTER
pfm:    LD      r5, r1, TUSE
        LDI     r0, 2                   ; rxframe returns to pfmc
        ST      r0, r1, STATE
        JMP     rxframe
pfmc:   BT      pfmto
        BNZ     pfmto                   ; an invalid frame counts as no reply
        LD      r0, r1, HDR
        CMPI    r0, T_RPFM
        BNZ     seenv                   ; another valid frame: as IDLE would
        LD      r2, r1, HDR + 1
        LD      r3, r1, TS
        CMP     r2, r3
        BNZ     idle
        LD      r0, r1, HDR + 2         ; a reply for us: NS = its source,
        ST      r0, r1, NS              ; PS = TS, TokenCount = 0, pass
        LDI     r0, 0
        ST      r0, r1, TC
        ST      r3, r1, PS
        JMP     passtk
pfmto:  LD      r2, r1, NS              ; no reply
        LD      r3, r1, TS
        CMP     r2, r3
        BNZ     passtk                  ; a successor is known: pass to it
        LD      r3, r1, PS              ; r3 = (PS + 1) mod (Nmax_master + 1)
        INC     r3
        LD      r0, r1, NMAX
        CMP     r0, r3
        BC      np2
        LDI     r3, 0
np2:
        CMP     r3, r2
        BNZ     poll                    ; poll the next address
        ; Every address polled and none answered: the sole master. It
        ; uses the token, then polls the ring again.

; -------------------------------------------------------------- USE_TOKEN
usetok: SETD    0                       ; TD = NOW: the WAITB is a test
        WAITB   INQ_NE, T
        BT      donetk
        .bounded "the WAITB INQ_NE, T just before completed by its condition, and only this thread pops its INQ"
        POP     r4                      ; DA | n << 8
        MOV     r3, r4
        SHLI    r3, 8
        SHRI    r3, 8
        SHRI    r4, 8
        MOV     r2, r1
        ADDI    r2, BUF
        MOV     r5, r4
ucopy:  POP     r0                      ; the host sends the rest promptly
        ST      r0, r2, 0
        INC     r2
        DJNZ    r5, ucopy
        SETD    0
        LDI     r2, T_DNER
        CALL    txframe
        LDIH    r3, 0x40
        WAITB   OUTQ_NF, T              ; TD has passed: a test
        BT      donetk
        .bounded "the WAITB OUTQ_NF, T just before completed by its condition, so OUTQ has room"
        PUSH    r3                      ; 0x40dd: sent

; --------------------------------------------------------- DONE_WITH_TOKEN
; Nmax_info_frames is 1, so the token is done with after one frame. With
; no successor known, poll from TS + 1. Otherwise pass the token, but
; every Npoll tokens poll one address between TS and NS first (the
; maintenance poll that finds a master that has come up since).
donetk: LD      r2, r1, NS
        LD      r3, r1, TS
        CMP     r2, r3
        BZ      pollts
        LD      r3, r1, TC
        INC     r3
        ST      r3, r1, TC
        LD      r0, r1, NPOLL
        CMP     r3, r0                  ; C: TokenCount + 1 >= Npoll
        BNC     passtk
        LD      r3, r1, PS              ; r3 = (PS + 1) mod (Nmax_master + 1)
        INC     r3
        LD      r0, r1, NMAX
        CMP     r0, r3
        BC      np3
        LDI     r3, 0
np3:
        CMP     r3, r2
        BNZ     poll                    ; PS + 1 is not NS: poll it
        LD      r0, r1, TS              ; the poll cycle is complete
        ST      r0, r1, PS
        LDI     r0, 1
        ST      r0, r1, TC

; ------------------------------------------------------------- PASS_TOKEN
; Any frame that starts within Tusage_timeout shows the token was taken;
; it is received and handled as in IDLE. Silence: send it once more, then
; give the successor up and poll from NS + 1.
passtk: LDI     r0, 0
        ST      r0, r1, RETRY
ptx:    LDI     r2, T_TOKEN
        LD      r3, r1, NS
        LDI     r4, 0
        CALL    txframe
        LD      r5, r1, TUSE
        LDI     r0, 3                   ; rxframe returns to ptxc
        ST      r0, r1, STATE
        JMP     rxframe
ptxc:   BNT     seen
        LD      r0, r1, RETRY
        TEST    r0, r0
        BNZ     ptfail
        INC     r0
        ST      r0, r1, RETRY
        JMP     ptx
ptfail: LD      r0, r1, NS
        ST      r0, r1, PS
        JMP     lostps


; ---------------------------------------------------------------- rxframe
; Receive one frame (the Receive Frame state machine), entered by JMP with
; STATE set (see rfret). The first octet must
; start within r5 ticks of TD; later octets within Tframe_abort of the one
; before; the first one, within r5 ticks of the entry (the line is first
; seen at mark, so the master may come here late, inside the stop bit
; before). Returns T = 1: silence, nothing came. Else T = 0 and Z = 1 for a
; valid frame (its header at HDR; the data of a frame for TS or 255 went to
; OUTQ, then its status), Z = 0 for an invalid one (a broken preamble, a
; bad header CRC, a bad data CRC or an octet missing).
rxframe: MOV    r6, r5
        SETD    1                       ; re-anchor: the silence counts from here
rfm:    WAITD   1                       ; the line at mark first (the stop bit of
        IN      r0                      ; the frame before, or idle), sampled
        TEST    r0, r0                  ; once a tick
        BNZ     rfst
        DJNZ    r6, rfm
        LDI     r0, 4
        CSRW    FLAGS, r0               ; T = 1: silence
        JMP     rfret
rfst:   CALL    rbs                     ; the first octet's start bit, in time r6
        JMP     rfgot
rfhunt: CALL    rxbyte
rfgot:  BT      rfret                   ; silence
        LDI     r6, 0x55
        CMP     r0, r6
        BNZ     rfhunt                  ; octets before a preamble are eaten
        LD      r5, r1, TABRT
        CALL    rxbyte
        BT      rfbad
        LDI     r6, 0xFF
        CMP     r0, r6
        BNZ     rfbad
        LDI     r7, 0                   ; the CRC unit for the header CRC-8:
        LDIH    r7, 0x81                ; x^8 + x^7 + 1 left-aligned, preset
        CSRW    CRC_POLY, r7            ; 0xFF (a write of CRC presets it)
        LDIH    r7, 0xFF
        CSRW    CRC, r7
        MOV     r2, r1
        ADDI    r2, HDR
        LDI     r3, 6
rfh:    CALL    rxbyte                  ; type, DA, SA, length (MSB first), CRC
        BT      rfbad
        ST      r0, r2, 0
        INC     r2
        DJNZ    r3, rfh
        STCRC   r0
        MOV16   r6, 0xAA00              ; rev8(0x55): the CRC-8 residue
        CMP     r0, r6
        BNZ     rfbad                   ; a bad header CRC: ignored
        LD      r4, r1, HDR + 3
        SWAP    r4, r4
        LD      r0, r1, HDR + 4
        OR      r4, r4, r0
        BZ      rfret                   ; no data: valid
        MOV16   r7, 0x1021              ; the CRC unit for the data CRC-16:
        CSRW    CRC_POLY, r7            ; x^16 + x^12 + x^5 + 1, preset 0xFFFF
        LDI     r7, 0
        NOT     r7, r7
        CSRW    CRC, r7
        LD      r0, r1, HDR + 1         ; r3 = 0 (from DJNZ): report it
        LD      r6, r1, TS
        CMP     r0, r6
        BZ      rfd
        LDI     r6, 0xFF
        CMP     r0, r6
        BZ      rfd
        LDI     r3, 1                   ; not for us: only checked
rfd:    ADDI    r4, 2                   ; the data, then its CRC (LSB first)
rfdb:   CALL    rxbyte
        BT      rfbad
        TEST    r3, r3
        BNZ     rfnext
        CMPI    r4, 3
        BNC     rfnext                  ; a CRC octet: not reported
        WAITB   OUTQ_NF, T              ; TD has passed: a test
        BT      rfnext
        .bounded "the WAITB OUTQ_NF, T just before completed by its condition, so OUTQ has room"
        PUSH    r0
rfnext: DJNZ    r4, rfdb
        STCRC   r6
        MOV16   r2, 0x1D0F              ; rev16(0xF0B8): the CRC-16 residue
        LDI     r0, 2
        CMP     r6, r2
        BZ      rfrep
        LDI     r0, 3                   ; 3: bit 14, the data CRC is bad
rfrep:  TEST    r3, r3
        BNZ     rfchk
        SHLI    r0, 6
        LD      r6, r1, HDR
        ANDI    r6, 0x3F
        OR      r0, r0, r6
        SWAP    r0, r0
        LD      r6, r1, HDR + 2
        OR      r0, r0, r6
        WAITB   OUTQ_NF, T
        BT      rfchk
        .bounded "the WAITB OUTQ_NF, T just before completed by its condition, so OUTQ has room"
        PUSH    r0                      ; the status
rfchk:  STCRC   r6
        CMP     r6, r2                  ; Z: the data CRC is good
        JMP     rfret

; Past thread 2's entry (0x100 .. 0x10F).
        .org    0x110
rfbad:  LDI     r0, 0
        CSRW    FLAGS, r0               ; T = 0, Z = 0: invalid
; Back to the state that asked, by STATE (1 IDLE, 2 POLL_FOR_MASTER, 3
; PASS_TOKEN). Not a CALL: the deadline checker returns every RET to every
; CALL, and a RET here would close a loop with no deadline on it. LD and
; DJNZ leave T and Z alone.
rfret:  LD      r0, r1, STATE
        DJNZ    r0, rfr2
        JMP     idlec
rfr2:   DJNZ    r0, rfr3
        JMP     pfmc
rfr3:   JMP     ptxc

; ----------------------------------------------------------------- rxbyte
; One 8N1 octet, LSB first, through SHI (so into the CRC). TD is the
; middle of the last data bit of the octet before (or the end of the last
; stop bit sent); the start bit must come within r5 ticks of the middle of
; that octet's stop bit. The search samples RX through IN once a tick
; (eight times a bit, as a UART does). Returns T = 1 if it did not come;
; else T = 0, the octet in r0 and TD at the middle of its last data bit.
rxbyte: WAITD   OVS                     ; the middle of the stop bit
        MOV     r6, r5
rbs:    WAITD   1
        IN      r0
        TEST    r0, r0
        BZ      rbgo                    ; low: a start bit
        DJNZ    r6, rbs
        LDI     r0, 4
        CSRW    FLAGS, r0               ; T = 1: silence
        RET
rbgo:   WAITD   3                       ; 3 to 4 ticks after its edge
        LDI     r0, 8
        CSRW    CNT, r0
rbit:   WAITD   OVS
        SHI
        BNZ     rbit
        LDI     r0, 0
        CSRW    FLAGS, r0               ; T = 0
        STSR    r0
        SHRI    r0, 8
        RET

; ---------------------------------------------------------------- txframe
; Send a frame of type r2 to station r3 with r4 data octets from CFG + BUF
; (r4 = 0: none, and no data CRC). The driver goes on Tturnaround (40 bit
; times, and one more to spare) after the end of the last stop bit
; received (TD, the middle of its last data bit, + 1.5 bits), then one bit
; ahead of the preamble, and off at the end of the last stop bit.
txframe: WAITD  180                     ; TD is the middle of a last data
        WAITD   160                     ; bit, as sampled (up to a tick early):
                                        ; 1.5 + 40 bit times and a bit to spare
        LDI     r0, 3
        OUT     r0                      ; DE on, TX mark
        LDI     r0, 0x55
        CALL    txbyte
        LDI     r0, 0xFF
        CALL    txbyte
        LDI     r7, 0                   ; the CRC unit for the header CRC-8:
        LDIH    r7, 0x81                ; x^8 + x^7 + 1 left-aligned, preset
        CSRW    CRC_POLY, r7            ; 0xFF (a write of CRC presets it)
        LDIH    r7, 0xFF
        CSRW    CRC, r7
        MOV     r0, r2
        CALL    txbyte                  ; type
        MOV     r0, r3
        CALL    txbyte                  ; DA
        LD      r0, r1, TS
        CALL    txbyte                  ; SA
        LDI     r0, 0
        CALL    txbyte                  ; length, MSB first
        MOV     r0, r4
        CALL    txbyte
        STCRC   r0
        REV     r0, r0
        NOT     r0, r0                  ; the header CRC, complemented
        CALL    txbyte
        TEST    r4, r4
        BZ      txend
        MOV16   r7, 0x1021              ; the CRC unit for the data CRC-16:
        CSRW    CRC_POLY, r7            ; x^16 + x^12 + x^5 + 1, preset 0xFFFF
        LDI     r7, 0
        NOT     r7, r7
        CSRW    CRC, r7
        MOV     r2, r1
        ADDI    r2, BUF
txd:    LD      r0, r2, 0
        INC     r2
        CALL    txbyte
        DJNZ    r4, txd
        STCRC   r0
        REV     r0, r0
        NOT     r0, r0                  ; the data CRC, complemented,
        MOV     r2, r0                  ; least significant octet first
        CALL    txbyte
        MOV     r0, r2
        SWAP    r0, r0
        CALL    txbyte
txend:  LDI     r0, 1
        WAITD   OVS                     ; the end of the last stop bit
        OUT     r0                      ; DE off
        RET

; txbyte: one 8N1 character of the octet in r0 bits 7:0 (bits 15:8 are
; never shifted out), its start bit OVS ticks after TD. OUT writes TX and
; DE (DE stays on), SHO writes TX alone.
txbyte: LDSR    r0
        LDI     r0, 8
        CSRW    CNT, r0
        LDI     r0, 2
        WAITD   OVS                     ; the stop bit before it ends
        OUT     r0                      ; start bit
tbit:   WAITD   OVS
        SHO                             ; a data bit, LSB first, into the CRC
        BNZ     tbit
        LDI     r0, 3
        WAITD   OVS
        OUT     r0                      ; the stop bit
        RET
